From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: amami: handle battery temperature as stock does

The SMBB charges at full current anywhere inside its BTC window, and the
driver's default window, [35%:70%] of the thermistor reference, ends at
about 40C on this battery: on a warm day the pack sits there and the phone
does not charge. Stock (Sony's 14.6.A kernel) leaves the window to the
hardware and derates in software: 650mA to 4.2V above 45C, 650mA below
10C. Use the extended hot edge, keep the narrow cold one so it never
charges below freezing, and derate as stock does (needs 0119, and 0071 for
the thermistor).

An earlier version set qcom,jeita-extended-temp-range on the reading that
the battery was too hot at room temperature. It was not at room
temperature: the same reading is 42C on the battery thermistor's own
table, and the extended range on both edges, with no derating, charged at
1.3A to 4.35V up to about 57C and down to about -7C.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-rhine-amami.dts	2026-10-16 12:29:50.729408531 +0400
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-rhine-amami.dts	2026-10-16 12:30:04.748038993 +0400
@@ -125,6 +125,24 @@
 
 	monitored-battery = <&battery>;
 
+	/*
+	 * Battery temperature handled as Sony's stock kernel does. The hot
+	 * edge of the SMBB's window is the extended one, 25% of the
+	 * reference, about 57C on this battery's thermistor: the narrow 35%
+	 * stops charging at about 40C, where the battery sits on a warm day.
+	 * The cold edge stays at 70%, about 4C, so it never charges below
+	 * freezing. Stock does not set the edges and leaves them to the
+	 * hardware; these are chosen, not read. Between them, stock's
+	 * derating: 650mA to 4.2V above 45C, 650mA below 10C.
+	 */
+	qcom,battery-hot-threshold-percent = <25>;
+	qcom,battery-cold-threshold-percent = <70>;
+	qcom,warm-battery-decidegc = <450>;
+	qcom,cool-battery-decidegc = <100>;
+	qcom,warm-charge-current-limit = <650000>;
+	qcom,warm-charge-voltage-limit = <4200000>;
+	qcom,cool-charge-current-limit = <650000>;
+
 	io-channels = <&pm8941_vadc VADC_VBAT_SNS>;
 	io-channel-names = "vbat";
 
